# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
/.codex/

# image lab job log (cost metering, runtime data)
/var/

# Event promo material. Licensed stock photography, client-supplied portraits
# of real people, and supplied music stay out of the repository: pushing them
# would publish licensed and personal media into git history, which cannot be
# undone by a later delete. Partner logos (logos/) ARE committed — they are
# small, and the client cleared their use for this project.
#
# Regenerate from the material drop folder before rendering:
#   node labs/event/scripts/prepare-assets.mjs --src <dir> --slug <slug>
# Note that sake-2026's brief names these files, so a clone must run the script
# (or null the slots) before `npm run event:render` — Remotion fails a render on
# a missing image rather than silently dropping it, which is the behaviour we
# want: a slot is only "empty by design" when the brief says null.
/public/event/*/photos/
/public/event/*/art/
/public/event/*/bgm.mp3

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# python (blender scripts)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The default asset pool (lib/assets/defaults.ts) IS PART OF THE SYSTEM.
#
# Music, sound effects, stock pictures and marks ship with the code and deploy
# with it (owner, 2026-08-30). They are not content somebody uploaded and not a
# dataset kept somewhere else: a build that does not carry them is a build whose
# films have no sound, which is what 「サーバーで動かない」 means. A user's own
# uploads are the separate thing, and they live in R2 against a take.
#
# So the default here is COMMITTED, and every line below is an exception that
# has to state why it cannot be. Whenever an exception is resolved, delete the
# line — do not leave it as "we never got round to it".
#
# 効果音ラボ forbids redistributing the files themselves, and this repository is
# PUBLIC, so committing these would be the redistribution they forbid. This is
# the one exception that is a licence and not a decision. It ends when the
# repository stops being public, or when these are replaced by sounds that are
# ours (the same move that replaced the licensed stock photography).
# scripts/fetch-default-sfx.mjs restores them anywhere and the committed
# catalog.json records what belongs here; R2 `defaults/sfx/` is what the
# deployed app reads (`npm run sfx:sync`).
/public/defaults/sfx/*.mp3
# The footage the closing plate stands on, one clip per art direction. Supplied
# by the owner (the same two files the freehand lab used: Fuji above the clouds
# and a city at dusk), and their LICENCE HAS NOT BEEN CONFIRMED — a default
# asset's whole job is to be safe to burn into anybody's MP4, and git history
# cannot be taken back. Committed the day their source is known; until then the
# catalog says `licensed: false` and the renderer leaves them out
# (lib/assets/defaults.ts).
/public/defaults/video/*.mp4
#
# COMMITTED: public/defaults/{bgm,stills,portraits,marks,devices}/. Generated
# with Suno or Midjourney on commercial plans (or authored as code), so they are
# ours to redistribute — the whole point of replacing the licensed stock and the
# real people's portraits under public/event/. A generation recipe cannot
# restore them (the same prompt yields a different picture, and a different
# take), so the repository has to hold the bytes rather than the recipe.
#
# bgm/ was ignored until 2026-08-30 for a reason that had already been corrected
# once: it was called "unlicensed placeholders" and is not. Nothing then read
# the tracks on a deployed build, because Vercel builds from git.

# Walkthrough output: a real recording of a sample narration, regenerated on
# demand by `npm run event-cm:walkthrough`. Costs an LLM call and a TTS pass to
# make, and is a verification artefact rather than a default asset.
/public/walkthrough/
